        },
        "title": "Zero or One Authoritative Region",
        "answer": "The proposed invariant is simple: each viewport has zero or one authoritative focus region. Many nodes may be selected, pinned, highlighted, searched, hovered, or otherwise emphasized, but those states do not create additional focus regions. Focus remains singular so it can reliably answer where the user is currently working.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "One viewport, at most one focus region.",
        "notes": "Multiple simultaneous focus regions are possible in theory, but they weaken the meaning of focus and are not part of the initial model.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786462966587,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
