        "title": "Branch Expansion Can Move Focus Deeper",
        "answer": "When a user deliberately expands a branch, that branch can become the new focused region. The rest of the graph remains available as surrounding context, but the expanded branch receives semantic priority. Expanding again can move focus deeper. Leaving or backing out can restore focus to a parent region without requiring multiple active regions at the same time.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "Branch expansion acts like spatial navigation into a deeper working context.",
        "notes": "The exact gestures that acquire focus are still an interaction-design question; the underlying model should support this behavior regardless of gesture.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
