        "title": "Zoom Supplies the Default; Focus Supplies Context",
        "answer": "Zoom and focus are independent inputs. A centralized zoom-band resolver converts viewport scale into a base semantic band such as dot, glyph, icon, summary, or detail. Focus then tells the presentation system which nodes deserve promotion relative to that base. A graph may therefore be globally at glyph scale while nodes inside the focused branch render as icons or summaries.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "Zoom answers how far away. Focus answers what matters here.",
        "notes": "The zoom resolver should not know about branches. The focus model should not know about wheel thresholds or hysteresis.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786462966587,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
