        "title": "Start with One Authoritative Focus Record",
        "answer": "The launch-sized model only needs enough state to identify the current focused anchor and derive membership in its region. A conceptual record might contain focusedNodeId, branchRootId, and an optional mode. The important requirement is not the exact object shape; it is that the graph has one authoritative answer to what region is focused and can determine whether any node is focused, inside the focused region, or outside it.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "Store as little as necessary, but make the answer authoritative.",
        "notes": "A focus path or history can be added later without changing the zero-or-one active region invariant.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
