        "title": "Expose a Focus Relationship, Not Focus Policy Everywhere",
        "answer": "Consumers should be able to ask for a small relationship such as focused, in-region, or outside. The presentation resolver can combine that relationship with the base zoom band and explicit node state to choose a requested surface. Individual node renderers should not independently decide whether focus means icon, summary, detail, or something else.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "Compute focus relationship centrally; apply presentation policy centrally.",
        "notes": "A useful conceptual seam is getFocusRelation(nodeId) followed by resolvePresentation(baseBand, focusRelation, nodeState).",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
