        "title": "Yes: Focus Is a Legitimate Presentation Override",
        "answer": "Normal zoom establishes the default amount of information the viewport can support. Focus can promote nodes inside the active region beyond that default. For example, unrelated nodes might render as glyphs while the focused branch uses icons and the focused anchor uses summary. Explicitly opened content may use detail. These are not broken zoom states; they are context-driven presentation states.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "Distance sets the baseline. Attention can promote important content above it.",
        "notes": "Promotion should generally be easier than arbitrary contextual demotion. The graph should not become less informative merely because a node is focused.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
